           "text": "Electrical Logo FAQs",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h3",
           "text": "Should an electrician logo use a lightning bolt?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>A lightning bolt identifies the trade instantly, but it is very common. Logo Austin styles the symbol so it is distinctive, or explores alternatives such as plugs, circuits or monograms.</p>",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h3",
           "text": "Do you design logos for solar companies?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>Yes. Logo Austin designs logos for solar installers and renewable-energy businesses as well as electricians and electrical contractors.</p>",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h3",
           "text": "How much does a electrical logo cost?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>At Logo Austin, a custom electrical logo is priced from $125 to $175. There is no upfront charge; you pay only after approving the final design.</p>",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "heading",
           "level": "h3",
           "text": "How fast can I get my electrical logo?",
           "classes": []
          },
          {
           "t": "text",
           "html": "<p>Logo Austin usually delivers multiple electrical logo concepts the same day. Final files in JPG, PNG, SVG, PDF, AI and EPS follow as soon as you approve a design, with full ownership.</p>",
           "classes": []
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
